@page "/docs/accessibility/pointer-and-touch"

@* WCAG 2.5.8 target size (the sweep of Nov 10, 2026) and 2.5.7 dragging (inventory section 1.10), with
   what changes on touch screens (section 1.13). *@

<ArticlePage Section="accessibility" Slug="pointer-and-touch">
    <Lead>
        Targets are at least 24 by 24 pixels, or have room around them, as WCAG 2.2 asks; the one exception is listed
        below. Most drags can also be done with single clicks, through a button or a menu.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Target sizes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Buttons and icon buttons are at least 32 pixels tall, even at the small size. A checkbox, radio or switch is clicked
            through its whole label. Small icons inside a field or a tab, such as a clear button or a tab's close button, keep
            their small look but take clicks from a 24-pixel area around them.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            One control falls short of 24 pixels and relies on another way to do the same thing: the stacked step buttons of a
            <Anchor Href="docs/components/number-field">NumberField</Anchor>. Type the number instead, or set
            <Code>StepButtons="StepButtons.Split"</Code> for full-height buttons on each side.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">A way around every drag</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Dragging is hard or impossible for some users, so each drag has a single-click way to the same result:
        </TextBlock>
        <Table Items="Drags" Caption="Drags and their single-click alternatives" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params site-params-wrap" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Drag">@context!.Drag</TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Without dragging">@context!.Instead</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>

        <Heading Level="2">On touch screens</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>Fields use 16-pixel text on touch screens, so iOS doesn't zoom the page when one takes focus.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>Date fields open the phone's own date picker; one that needs IzzyBlazor's calendar shows its calendar button instead.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>File uploads drop the "or drag it here" text.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>One finger scrolls the page over a chart; two fingers pinch to zoom it.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>A carousel moves by swipe, and its arrows and dots still work.</ListItem>
            <ListItem>Toasts don't pause on touch, as there's no hover; error toasts stay until dismissed.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record DragAlternative(string Drag, string Instead);

    private static readonly DragAlternative[] Drags =
    [
        new("DataGrid: move or resize a column", "The column menu's Move left, Move right, Width and Fit to content items"),
        new("DataGrid: reorder rows", "The row handle's menu: Move up, Move down, Move to top, Move to bottom"),
        new("DataGrid: group by a column", "The column menu's Group by this column"),
        new("DataGrid: change the order of grouping levels", "Click a level's chip for its menu: Move left, Move right"),
        new("DataGrid: choose and order columns", "The column picker's checkboxes and each row's handle menu"),
        new("ListView and DropZoneGroup: move an item", "The handle's or the item's menu, including Move to another zone"),
        new("PickList: move items across", "The move buttons between the lists, or a double-click"),
        new("Scheduler: move or resize an appointment", "Click it and change its times in the form"),
        new("Splitter: resize a pane", "Click the bar for its menu: Wider, Narrower, Reset size and Collapse"),
        new("Chart: zoom and pan", "The Zoom in, Zoom out and Reset zoom buttons by the title; a ChartRangeSelector's preset ranges"),
        new("Carousel: swipe", "The previous and next buttons and the dots"),
        new("Slider, RangeSlider, ColorPanel", "Click where you want the value"),
        new("RangeSelector: move the window", "Click the strip, or choose a preset range"),
        new("FileUpload: drop a file", "The Choose a file link"),
    ];
}
